{
	title: 'Structured private user profile and intro preferences',
	spec: `USER.md in the Hal home is a short, human-readable Markdown briefing about the user, not a rigid configuration schema. It starts with # User and uses predictable optional fields: Name, Language preference, and Timezone. Optional sections Working preferences and Other durable context hold concise facts. Language preference distinguishes a default language or spelling variety from alternatives; a conversation in another language does not silently change the default. Timezone uses a valid IANA timezone identifier, not a fixed UTC offset. Unknown fields are omitted or explicitly Not specified, never invented or stored as angle-bracket placeholders. Existing freeform USER.md files remain valid and are included in prompts as before; no destructive migration or mandatory parser is introduced.

hal/intro asks for the user name when it is not already known and writes the supplied name to USER.md. Name, language preference, and timezone are skippable onboarding fields, asked one at a time; existing meaningful values are respected and skipped. A skipped field must not be asked again on resume. Placeholder or empty values do not count as a known name. Intro can offer an available client-reported IANA timezone for confirmation. A host timezone is only a labeled suggestion, especially when Hal runs on a remote server: it is never assumed to be the user timezone. With no trustworthy signal, ask or leave unknown; do not add location services or infer identity or location from account names, IP addresses, or credentials. No browser integration is required solely to obtain a timezone; use an already available signal or a simple question. Persist only supplied or confirmed values. Preserve the existing credential setup and resumable, provider-independent intro behavior.

Profile writes preserve user-authored content and existing facts. Adding a missing field must not truncate or rewrite the rest of the file; changes to an existing preference require an explicit user correction. Store only durable personal facts and preferences, never secrets, temporary progress, or project-specific requirements. Actual profile contents must never enter tracked tasks, examples, logs added for this feature, or commits. USER.md remains gitignored and protected by the project rebuild keep list; generic templates, if needed, contain no real profile data. The profile remains optional and its absence does not prevent normal operation.

Verify behavior with focused checks for missing and existing profiles, skipped fields across intro resume, preserving user-authored text, confirmed versus unconfirmed timezone suggestions, and the gitignore/rebuild protection. Prefer existing onboarding coverage and avoid tests that merely restate template text.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Intro uses optional Markdown field lines, not a profile schema: it preserves freeform text byte-for-byte and appends only supplied values. Blank, Not specified, unknown, N/A and angle-bracket placeholders do not count as known fields. Legacy About sections remain valid; new optional context uses Working preferences. SYSTEM.md describes the same private briefing format and explicit-correction rule.',
		'Name, language and timezone skips use the existing durable named answer records, so host recovery does not re-ask them. Timezone is a simple unprefilled question with Intl IANA validation: no browser integration, server timezone suggestion or automatic inference. Invalid timezone input is not written and can be corrected or skipped. Existing meaningful profile fields take precedence over replayed answers.'
	],
	needs: ['n2', 'vc'],
